{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "quarter-ice-perpetual-cycle",
  "title": "Quarter Ice Perpetual Cycle",
  "description": "A quarter-ice drill to work on both the high cycle and the low cycle, a modification of the Perpetual Cycle drill for smaller spaces or groups too large to keep everyone moving in the original. One line of skaters. P1 dumps the puck in to the bottom corner, goes down to retrieve it and walks it along the bottom boards. P2 swings down behind the net, following a bit behind. P1 bounces the puck off the boards and back, and P2 picks it up. P1 continues around the circle and attacks the net, turning toward it as the pass arrives; P2 takes a few steps and passes to P1, who shoots. Then the same thing in mirror image on the other net: P3 dumps the puck in on the other side, P2 loops back into the zone and retrieves it, P3 follows up and receives the bounce, and passes out front to P2, who shoots. The drill repeats.",
  "tags": [
    "cycle",
    "passing",
    "shooting",
    "offence"
  ],
  "rink": "half-right",
  "source": {
